commit 436bd933f37173efa083cd4fdcdc301b666ce200
Author: Craig Tiller <ctiller@google.com>
Date:   Mon Jan 31 16:47:33 2022 +0000

    Rewrite reclaimer queue (#28698)

    Backport of https://github.com/grpc/grpc/pull/28698, first released in
    gRPC 1.45.0, to gRPC 1.43.0. Only the two source files are taken; the
    test change is left out because the gRPC tests are not built here.

    In 1.43.0 ReclaimerQueue::Cancel() frees the entry but leaves its index
    in queue_, and only the reclamation loop pops queue_, which runs only
    while the memory quota is overcommitted. Under the default unlimited
    quota every new connection therefore leaves up to 4 indices behind for
    the life of the process. The rewrite removes cancelled reclaimers from
    the queue as they are cancelled.

